Proteins are a diverse group of molecular structures, consisting of a diverse range of amino acids and alkyl chains. The existence of several protein structures is often evidence of a distinct function in the biological system. The smaller and more complex the protein, the higher its species diversity. All proteins are classified as nucleic acid molecules, and are linear array of DNA adducts, which are either single-stranded or double-stranded.

The many types of proteins are classified into three major groups: milk proteins, animal proteins, and plant proteins. Each protein structure has different molecular structures and different functions;
